/* 
time complexity - o(n)
space complexity - o(1)
INTUITION 
Every number points to an index (value → index).

When you visit a number, go to the index it represents.

If the value at that index is already negative, it means you have visited this index before → the number is a duplicate.

Otherwise, mark that index as visited by flipping it to negative.

First index that is already negative = the duplicate.
*/
class Solution {
    public int findDuplicate(int[] nums) {
        for(int i=0 ;i<nums.length ; i++){
            int idx = Math.abs(nums[i])-1;
            if(nums[idx] < 0){
                return Math.abs(nums[i]);
            }
            nums[idx]*=-1;
        }
        return -1;
    }
}
